From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:28:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: read the client's size hint flags

get_size_hints tests the supplied mask from XGetWMNormalHints, which lists
the fields the property format holds and is 0x3ff for any current client.
Since 6bda0eec accepted zero positions, a static gravity window at a
nonnegative position counts as positioned even without PPosition, so a
maximized skip-taskbar popup becomes a dropdown. RPG Maker games using
Fullscreen++, such as Waste Walkers (371100), map a black maximized
backdrop that gets painted over the game as the override, leaving the
screen black.

Use hints.flags instead. Wine sets PPosition on every window that is not
minimized or maximized, so maximized and minimized Wine windows stop
qualifying through this check.
---
 src/steamcompmgr.cpp | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
index 8d4f5a3..c168398 100644
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -5752,10 +5752,12 @@ get_win_type(xwayland_ctx_t *ctx, steamcompmgr_win_t *w)
 static void
 get_size_hints(xwayland_ctx_t *ctx, steamcompmgr_win_t *w)
 {
-	XSizeHints hints;
-	long hintsSpecified = 0;
+	XSizeHints hints = {};
+	long hintsSupplied = 0;
 
-	XGetWMNormalHints(ctx->dpy, w->xwayland().id, &hints, &hintsSpecified);
+	// Xlib's supplied mask lists the fields the property can hold, not the ones the client set.
+	XGetWMNormalHints(ctx->dpy, w->xwayland().id, &hints, &hintsSupplied);
+	const long hintsSpecified = hints.flags;
 
 	const bool bHasPositionAndGravityHints = ( hintsSpecified & ( PPosition | PWinGravity ) ) == ( PPosition | PWinGravity );
 	if ( bHasPositionAndGravityHints &&
